IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc2-prohibited-acts`

-- ccc2-tests-prohibited-acts.l4 -- tests for ccc2-prohibited-acts.l4 (ss 49 to 56). Expected values are written beside each assertion from the text
-- of the provision, before the run. The s 787(1) penalty is a seam input from another part: the tests pass a placeholder that states nothing
-- (`no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`), so no assertion here says anything about s 787(1).

§ `Tests -- section 49 (repealed)`

#ASSERT `s 49 as the text shows it` EQUALS "49 [Repealed, 2018, c. 29, s. 1]"

§ `Tests -- section 50, assisting alien enemy to leave Canada, or omitting to prevent treason (lines 891-899)`

-- (1)(a): incites or wilfully assists a subject of an enemy state to leave Canada without the consent of the Crown, unless the accused establishes that assistance to the state was not intended.
#ASSERT `s 50(1)(a) the person assists a subject of an enemy state to leave Canada` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 50(1)(a) the person assists a subject of an enemy state to leave Canada` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the accused establishes no assistance was intended: the "unless" is met
#ASSERT `s 50(1)(a) the person assists a subject of an enemy state to leave Canada` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no incitement or assistance
#ASSERT `s 50(1)(a) the person assists a subject of an enemy state to leave Canada` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a subject of some other state
#ASSERT `s 50(1)(a) the person assists a subject of an enemy state to leave Canada` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- with the consent of the Crown
-- (1)(b): knowing that a person is about to commit high treason or treason, does not inform a justice of the peace or other peace officer, or make other reasonable efforts to prevent it.
#ASSERT `s 50(1)(b) the person omits to prevent treason` TRUE FALSE NOTHING FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 50(1)(b) the person omits to prevent treason` FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no knowledge
#ASSERT `s 50(1)(b) the person omits to prevent treason` TRUE FALSE NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- made other reasonable efforts
#ASSERT `s 50(1)(b) the person omits to prevent treason` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- informed a peace officer
#ASSERT `s 50(1)(b) the person omits to prevent treason` TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- informed someone who is not an officer: not what the paragraph asks
#ASSERT `s 50(1)(b) the person omits to prevent treason` TRUE TRUE NOTHING FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the informed person's status is left open by s 2 "peace officer includes"
-- the same duty as a regulative rule, run on the stable binary (a DEONTIC cannot be compared with EQUALS; the outcomes are printed and recorded in NOTES.md):
-- informing in time -> FULFILLED; other reasonable efforts -> FULFILLED; nothing done -> the two alternatives stay standing (the text states no deadline).
#TRACE `s 50(1)(b) the duty to inform or to make other reasonable efforts` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the accused` DOES `s 50(1)(b) informs a justice of the peace or other peace officer` AT 1
#TRACE `s 50(1)(b) the duty to inform or to make other reasonable efforts` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the accused` DOES `s 50(1)(b) makes other reasonable efforts to prevent the commission of the treason` AT 1
#TRACE `s 50(1)(b) the duty to inform or to make other reasonable efforts` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 5
-- (2): indictable, imprisonment not exceeding fourteen years.
#ASSERT `s 50(2) the class of the offence under subsection 50(1)` EQUALS `an indictable offence`
#ASSERT `s 50(2) the punishment for an offence under subsection 50(1)` EQUALS LIST Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

§ `Tests -- section 51, intimidating Parliament or legislature (lines 900-901)`

#ASSERT `s 51 the person intimidates Parliament or the legislature of a province` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 51 the person intimidates Parliament or the legislature of a province` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no act of violence
#ASSERT `s 51 the person intimidates Parliament or the legislature of a province` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- violence for another purpose
#ASSERT `s 51 the class of the offence` EQUALS `an indictable offence`
#ASSERT `s 51 the punishment` EQUALS LIST Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

§ `Tests -- section 52, sabotage (lines 902-918)`

-- (2) prohibited act means an act or omission that (a) impairs the efficiency ... or (b) causes property to be lost, damaged or destroyed.
#ASSERT `s 52(2) the act or omission is a prohibited act` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 52(2) the act or omission is a prohibited act` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 52(2) the act or omission is a prohibited act` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 52(2) the act or omission is a prohibited act` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "means"
-- (3)(a), (b), (c) and (4): "No person does a prohibited act ... by reason only that ..."
#ASSERT `s 52(3)(a) the person does a prohibited act by reason only of stopping work over a failure to agree with the employer` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 52(3)(a) the person does a prohibited act by reason only of stopping work over a failure to agree with the employer` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 52(3)(b) the person does a prohibited act by reason only of stopping work over a failure of the employer and a bargaining agent to agree` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 52(3)(b) the person does a prohibited act by reason only of stopping work over a failure of the employer and a bargaining agent to agree` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 52(3)(c) the person does a prohibited act by reason only of stopping work as a result of taking part in a combination for reasonable protection` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 52(3)(c) the person does a prohibited act by reason only of stopping work as a result of taking part in a combination for reasonable protection` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 52(4) the person does a prohibited act by reason only of attending at or near a dwelling-house or place to obtain or communicate information` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 52(4) the person does a prohibited act by reason only of attending at or near a dwelling-house or place to obtain or communicate information` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (5): participating in advocacy, protest or dissent without intending any of the harms in (1)(a) and (b): no offence.
#ASSERT `s 52(5) the person commits an offence under subsection 52(1) while participating in advocacy, protest or dissent` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 52(5) the person commits an offence under subsection 52(1) while participating in advocacy, protest or dissent` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- with the intent, the subsection is silent
#ASSERT `s 52(5) the person commits an offence under subsection 52(1) while participating in advocacy, protest or dissent` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (1): does a prohibited act with the intent to endanger (a) the safety, security or defence of Canada, or (b) the safety or security of forces of another state lawfully present in Canada.
--                                                          impairs damages stopA stopB stopC info  protest intentA intentB
#ASSERT `s 52(1) the person commits sabotage` TRUE  FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE  FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- impairs a thing, intends to endanger Canada's safety
#ASSERT `s 52(1) the person commits sabotage` FALSE TRUE  FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE  EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- damages property, intends to endanger allied forces
#ASSERT `s 52(1) the person commits sabotage` TRUE  FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING     -- a prohibited act with no intent to endanger
#ASSERT `s 52(1) the person commits sabotage` TRUE  FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE  FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- protest, no intent: subsection (5)
#ASSERT `s 52(1) the person commits sabotage` TRUE  FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE  TRUE  FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- protest with the intent: subsection (5) does not reach it
#ASSERT `s 52(1) the person commits sabotage` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE  TRUE  EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- not a prohibited act: "means"
#ASSERT `s 52(1) the person commits sabotage` TRUE  FALSE TRUE  FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE  FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- only stopping work over a failure to agree (3)(a)
#ASSERT `s 52(1) the person commits sabotage` TRUE  FALSE FALSE TRUE  FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE  FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- (3)(b)
#ASSERT `s 52(1) the person commits sabotage` TRUE  FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE  FALSE FALSE TRUE  FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- (3)(c)
#ASSERT `s 52(1) the person commits sabotage` TRUE  FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE  FALSE TRUE  FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- (4)
#ASSERT `s 52(1) the class of the offence of sabotage` EQUALS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`
#ASSERT `s 52(1) the punishment for sabotage` (Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`) EQUALS LIST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`), (Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)

§ `Tests -- section 52.1, sabotage of essential infrastructure (lines 919-945)`

-- (2) essential infrastructure means a facility or system ... that provides ... essential services, including (a) to (h), and (i) any other prescribed by regulations.
--                                                                  kind                                                    facility essential prescribed
#ASSERT `s 52.1(2) the facility or system is an essential infrastructure` `s 52.1(2) infrastructure of another kind` TRUE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 52.1(2) the facility or system is an essential infrastructure` `s 52.1(2)(a) transportation infrastructure` TRUE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 52.1(2) the facility or system is an essential infrastructure` `s 52.1(2)(a) transportation infrastructure` FALSE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING   -- "including the following": a listed kind that fails the general test is not answered
#ASSERT `s 52.1(2) the facility or system is an essential infrastructure` `s 52.1(2)(h) financial infrastructure` TRUE FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 52.1(2) the facility or system is an essential infrastructure` `s 52.1(2) infrastructure of another kind` FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (i) prescribed by regulations
#ASSERT `s 52.1(2) the facility or system is an essential infrastructure` `s 52.1(2) infrastructure of another kind` FALSE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING   -- regulations are not among the sources
#ASSERT `s 52.1(2) the facility or system is an essential infrastructure` `s 52.1(2) infrastructure of another kind` TRUE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 52.1(2) the facility or system is an essential infrastructure` `s 52.1(2) infrastructure of another kind` FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "means"
#ASSERT `s 52.1(2) the facility or system is an essential infrastructure` `s 52.1(2) infrastructure of another kind` TRUE FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (1) and (3) to (5).
--                                                                          act   ei              intA   intB   intC   stopA stopB stopC info  protest
#ASSERT `s 52.1(1) the person commits sabotage of an essential infrastructure` TRUE (JUST TRUE)  TRUE  FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 52.1(1) the person commits sabotage of an essential infrastructure` TRUE (JUST TRUE)  FALSE FALSE TRUE  FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (c) a serious risk to public health or safety
#ASSERT `s 52.1(1) the person commits sabotage of an essential infrastructure` TRUE (JUST TRUE)  FALSE TRUE  FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (b)
#ASSERT `s 52.1(1) the person commits sabotage of an essential infrastructure` TRUE (JUST TRUE)  FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING     -- no intent
#ASSERT `s 52.1(1) the person commits sabotage of an essential infrastructure` TRUE (JUST TRUE)  TRUE  FALSE FALSE TRUE  FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE    -- (3)(a)
#ASSERT `s 52.1(1) the person commits sabotage of an essential infrastructure` TRUE (JUST TRUE)  TRUE  FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE  FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE    -- (3)(b)
#ASSERT `s 52.1(1) the person commits sabotage of an essential infrastructure` TRUE (JUST TRUE)  TRUE  FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE  FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE    -- (3)(c)
#ASSERT `s 52.1(1) the person commits sabotage of an essential infrastructure` TRUE (JUST TRUE)  TRUE  FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE  FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE    -- (4)
#ASSERT `s 52.1(1) the person commits sabotage of an essential infrastructure` TRUE (JUST TRUE)  FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE  EQUALS JUST FALSE    -- (5): protest, no intent
#ASSERT `s 52.1(1) the person commits sabotage of an essential infrastructure` TRUE (JUST TRUE)  TRUE  FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE  EQUALS JUST TRUE     -- protest with the intent: (5) does not reach it
#ASSERT `s 52.1(1) the person commits sabotage of an essential infrastructure` TRUE (JUST FALSE) TRUE  FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not an essential infrastructure: "means"
#ASSERT `s 52.1(1) the person commits sabotage of an essential infrastructure` TRUE NOTHING     TRUE  FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING      -- the definition leaves it open
#ASSERT `s 52.1(1) the person commits sabotage of an essential infrastructure` FALSE (JUST TRUE) TRUE  FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING     -- no interference
#ASSERT `s 52.1(1) the class of the offence of sabotage of an essential infrastructure` EQUALS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`
#ASSERT `s 52.1(1) the punishment for sabotage of an essential infrastructure` (Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`) EQUALS LIST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`), (Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)

§ `Tests -- section 52.2, sabotage by device (lines 946-953)`

#ASSERT `s 52.2(3) the thing is a device` FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- a computer program as defined in subsection 342.1(2)
#ASSERT `s 52.2(3) the thing is a device` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- a device in the ordinary sense
#ASSERT `s 52.2(3) the thing is a device` TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 52.2(3) the thing is a device` FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING   -- "includes": not otherwise defined
#ASSERT `s 52.2(3) the thing is a device` FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
--                                                    acts  device answer   intending knowing
#ASSERT `s 52.2(1) the person commits the device offence` TRUE (JUST TRUE) TRUE  FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- intending that it be used
#ASSERT `s 52.2(1) the person commits the device offence` TRUE (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE  EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- knowing that it will be used
#ASSERT `s 52.2(1) the person commits the device offence` TRUE (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 52.2(1) the person commits the device offence` FALSE (JUST TRUE) TRUE  TRUE  EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 52.2(1) the person commits the device offence` TRUE NOTHING     TRUE  TRUE  EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 52.2(1) the person commits the device offence` TRUE (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE  EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 52.2(2) the class of the offence under subsection 52.2(1)` EQUALS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`
#ASSERT `s 52.2(2) the punishment for an offence under subsection 52.2(1)` (Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`) EQUALS LIST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`), (Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)

§ `Tests -- section 52.3, Attorney General's consent (lines 954-955)`

#ASSERT `s 52.3 the proceeding is barred without the Attorney General's consent` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 52.3 the proceeding is barred without the Attorney General's consent` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- consent given: the bar is not engaged, and the text does not say the proceeding may go ahead
#ASSERT `s 52.3 the proceeding is barred without the Attorney General's consent` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- another offence

§ `Tests -- sections 53 to 56 (lines 956-970)`

#ASSERT `s 53 the person incites to mutiny` `s 53(a) attempts, for a traitorous or mutinous purpose, to seduce a member of the Canadian Forces from his duty and allegiance to Her Majesty` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 53 the person incites to mutiny` `s 53(a) attempts, for a traitorous or mutinous purpose, to seduce a member of the Canadian Forces from his duty and allegiance to Her Majesty` FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- no traitorous or mutinous purpose
#ASSERT `s 53 the person incites to mutiny` `s 53(b) attempts to incite or to induce a member of the Canadian Forces to commit a traitorous or mutinous act` FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- paragraph (b) names no purpose
#ASSERT `s 53 the person incites to mutiny` `s 53(b) attempts to incite or to induce a member of the Canadian Forces to commit a traitorous or mutinous act` FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING   -- not shown to be a member of the Canadian Forces
#ASSERT `s 53 the person incites to mutiny` `s 53(b) attempts to incite or to induce a member of the Canadian Forces to commit a traitorous or mutinous act` FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 53 the person incites to mutiny` `s 53 an act that is neither of those in paragraphs (a) and (b)` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 53 the class of the offence` EQUALS `an indictable offence`
#ASSERT `s 53 the punishment` EQUALS LIST Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`
#ASSERT `s 54 the person assists a deserter` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 54 the person assists a deserter` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- does not know
#ASSERT `s 54 the person assists a deserter` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 54 the class of the offence` EQUALS `an offence punishable on summary conviction`
#ASSERT `s 54 the punishment` (Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`) EQUALS LIST (Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)
#ASSERT `s 54 the proceedings are barred without the consent of the Attorney General of Canada` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 54 the proceedings are barred without the consent of the Attorney General of Canada` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 54 the proceedings are barred without the consent of the Attorney General of Canada` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 55: the offence charged is tested by its section number: 47 and 50 to 53 are in; 46, 48, 49 and 54 are not.
#ASSERT `s 55 evidence of an overt act is not admissible` (`Provision of the Code` OF 47, "") FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 55 evidence of an overt act is not admissible` (`Provision of the Code` OF 47, "") TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the overt act is set out in the indictment
#ASSERT `s 55 evidence of an overt act is not admissible` (`Provision of the Code` OF 47, "") FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- otherwise relevant to an overt act set out in the indictment
#ASSERT `s 55 evidence of an overt act is not admissible` (`Provision of the Code` OF 50, "(1)") FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- lower end of "sections 50 to 53"
#ASSERT `s 55 evidence of an overt act is not admissible` (`Provision of the Code` OF 52.1, "(1)") FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- between 52 and 53 in the Code's order
#ASSERT `s 55 evidence of an overt act is not admissible` (`Provision of the Code` OF 53, "") FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- upper end
#ASSERT `s 55 evidence of an overt act is not admissible` (`Provision of the Code` OF 49, "") FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- just below
#ASSERT `s 55 evidence of an overt act is not admissible` (`Provision of the Code` OF 54, "") FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- just above
#ASSERT `s 55 evidence of an overt act is not admissible` (`Provision of the Code` OF 46, "(1)") FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the text names section 47, not section 46
#ASSERT `s 55 evidence of an overt act is not admissible` (`Provision of the Code` OF 48, "(1)") FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 56:
#ASSERT `s 56 the person commits an offence in relation to a member of the R.C.M.P.` `s 56(a) persuades or counsels a member of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police to desert or absent himself without leave` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 56 the person commits an offence in relation to a member of the R.C.M.P.` `s 56(a) persuades or counsels a member of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police to desert or absent himself without leave` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not wilfully
#ASSERT `s 56 the person commits an offence in relation to a member of the R.C.M.P.` `s 56(b) aids, assists, harbours or conceals a member of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police who he knows is a deserter or absentee without leave` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 56 the person commits an offence in relation to a member of the R.C.M.P.` `s 56(b) aids, assists, harbours or conceals a member of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police who he knows is a deserter or absentee without leave` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- does not know
#ASSERT `s 56 the person commits an offence in relation to a member of the R.C.M.P.` `s 56(c) aids or assists a member of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police to desert or absent himself without leave, knowing that the member is about to desert or absent himself without leave` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 56 the person commits an offence in relation to a member of the R.C.M.P.` `s 56(c) aids or assists a member of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police to desert or absent himself without leave, knowing that the member is about to desert or absent himself without leave` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 56 the person commits an offence in relation to a member of the R.C.M.P.` `s 56 an act that is none of those in paragraphs (a) to (c)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 56 the class of the offence` EQUALS `an offence punishable on summary conviction`
#ASSERT `s 56 the punishment` (Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`) EQUALS LIST (Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)
